<h3>Warm-up: four original divide-by-eight facts</h3><table class="source-chart"><tbody><tr><td>80 ÷ 8</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>72 ÷ 8</td><td>9</td></tr><tr><td>96 ÷ 8</td><td>12</td></tr><tr><td>96 ÷ 4</td><td>24</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h3>Activity 1: exactly four problems to choose and solve</h3>
<ol><li><b>Mandatory entrance</b>: $9 per person, you + six others, 7 × $9 = <b>$63</b>.</li>
<li><b>Choose ONE time activity</b>: pumpkin weigh-off 11:12 AM to12:25 PM (<b>73 minutes</b>), OR carnival duration48min and departure12:10 PM (<b>arrival11:22 AM</b>).</li>
<li><b>Choose ONE quantity activity</b>: 7 sheep share91L/day (<b>13L each</b>), OR butter cow273kg weighs277kg less than actual cow (<b>550kg</b>).</li>
<li><b>Mandatory corn</b>: 54 ears in9 equal rows = <b>6 ears each</b>.</li></ol>
<p>Show the FOUR selected source problems and mathematical reasoning on a poster, including diagrams, equation and correct units. Student chooses path and presentation; do not impose all six options.</p>
<h3>Activity 2: Gallery walk</h3><p>Find one classmates' strategy DIFFERENT from yours and explain its difference. Record AT LEAST THREE features from posters that make the math easy to follow. Teacher checks real comparisons and presentation, not only typed answers.</p>
<p>The original section summary adds review:84L total,12L per seedling => 7 seedlings; it is not a fifth mandated fair problem. Publisher photographs, restricted Cool-down and original pupil PDF are not copied.</p></section>